WEBVTT

00:11:28.792 --> 00:11:30.042
Don't look at me.

00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:32.351
I think that's interesting --

00:11:32.375 --> 00:11:35.934
EP: But you understand what I'm saying?
It's in the small things like this,

00:11:35.958 --> 00:11:37.309
where the power of somebody

00:11:37.333 --> 00:11:39.518
is the power to make you feel
that you matter.

00:11:39.542 --> 00:11:40.934
We are creatures of meaning.

00:11:40.958 --> 00:11:43.601
It's the power to make you
feel like you're irrelevant.

00:11:43.625 --> 00:11:46.643
And I think that who has
the power is often that,

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:50.292
and that can be performed
by the one who pretends to care less.

00:11:52.042 --> 00:11:54.934
AG: So I want to come back
to the question that I asked you.

00:11:54.958 --> 00:11:57.809
EP: Like you have more to lose than me,
those kinds of game.

00:11:57.833 --> 00:12:00.268
I mean, power games are fascinating.